Changes in this fork (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

This is a fork of TensorFold 0.6.6 (upstream commit cb2ebf0; first forked from 0.6.3, 9356df5) by BertholomusAI (Albert Lee,
https://github.com/bertholomus), Copyright 2026. It adds the deepseek_v41 model family for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, tensor-parallel over two NVIDIA GB10
nodes. TensorFold's text above, LICENSE, LICENSES/ and the upstream sections of THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are unchanged.

Added:
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/   the model family (engine, kernels, server integration)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/rdma.py, src/tensorfold/cuda/rdma_gather.cu   RDMA-write all-gather for TP decode
  tools/dsv41/                             tests, checks, benchmark clients, the reference model, DESIGN.md,
                                           REPORT.md and ATTRIBUTION.md
  A "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on CUDA (TP2)" section in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and a fork note at the top of README.md.

Modified upstream files:
  pyproject.toml                               package data for the deepseek_v41 CUDA sources
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_grouped.cuh grouped EXL3 expert kernels extended (multi-row prompt-chunk kernels,
                                               a fused decode-window path)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.cu          as above
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.cpp         bindings for the added kernels
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.py          Python entry points for the added kernels
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_cb0.cu      template instantiations of the added kernels
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_cb1.cu      as above
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_cb2.cu      as above
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/prefill.py          optional tile choice by shape (TF_EXL3_PREFILL_TILES)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/linear.cu           shared helpers moved to linear_common.cuh (new); rot_in pinned to the
                                               same arithmetic; grouped decode linears in linear_grouped.cu (new)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/linear.cpp          bindings for the grouped linears
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/linear.py           Exl3Group and Exl3Linear.grouped(); extension renamed
  tests/cuda/test_exl3_experts.py              tests for the fused decode path
  src/tensorfold/cuda/http.py                  optional API key (TF_API_KEY / TF_API_KEY_FILE), all routes but /health;
                                               max_model_len in /v1/models
  src/tensorfold/cuda/server.py                a family's own image prompts continue through its vision object
  src/tensorfold/cuda/comm.py                  NCCL abort and asynchronous-error hooks (a concurrent lane's watchdog)
  src/tensorfold/serve_options.py              --vision for families with their own image path (CUDA_VISION)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/reply_text.py            DSML tool-call parsing for DeepSeek-V4.1
  src/tensorfold/server/request_options.py     reasoning_effort "off" heard as "none"
  src/tensorfold/server/authentication.py      the no-key startup line names the CUDA server's TF_API_KEY gate
  .gitignore                                   ignores macOS ._* files

The "git log" of this branch and tools/dsv41/ATTRIBUTION.md describe the changes and their sources.

The mistral-large-4-tp4 branch of this fork adds the mistral_large4 model family for Mistral Large 4, over four NVIDIA GB10
nodes, with the same holder and license.

Added:
  src/tensorfold/families/mistral_large4/  the model family (engine, kernels, server integration)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/load.py         the shard and rank-cache readers as a family-neutral import point
  tools/ml4/                               serve script, benchmark clients, DESIGN-CP4.md and ATTRIBUTION.md
  tools/ml4_step4_chat.py, tools/ml4_step6_conc.py, tools/parity/   the chat and tool-call set, a load sweep, parity tools
  tests/test_ml4_*.py                      tests of the family
  A "Mistral Large 4 on CUDA (four nodes)" section in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and a fork note at the top of README.md.

Modified upstream files, in addition to the list above:
  src/tensorfold/cli.py                        --tp above 2 for a family that declares it (CUDA_MAX_RANKS)
  src/tensorfold/cli_args.py                   as above
  src/tensorfold/cuda/comm.py                  all-to-all, a forked communicator, gather_done, threads on chosen cores
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_grouped.cuh int8 grouped expert kernels (mma m16n8k32) for prompt rounds
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.cu          as above; work lists built on the device
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.cpp         bindings for the added kernels
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.py          Python entry points for the added kernels
  src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/prefill.py          a wider default tile for prompt GEMMs (same bits)
  src/tensorfold/cuda/rdma_gather.cu           the proxy thread naps on a little core
  src/tensorfold/cuda/reply_text.py            Mistral tool calls ([TOOL_CALLS]name[ARGS]{json}) and hiding them
  src/tensorfold/cuda/server.py                think markers from the tokenizer, Mistral tool calls
  src/tensorfold/server/app.py                 think markers from the tokenizer
  src/tensorfold/server/text.py                [THINK] markers, Mistral tool-call markup
